## Context
DESIGN.md §4 PR-8, honoring R22 (+ verbs residue from v1 §2.8). Verified:
today's stop cancels one job and auto_build (default true) starts a fresh
build on the next query — the user has no durable veto. The PR: one persisted
pause row, written by `pause`, read before any scheduling decision — gates
build, auto_build, and background work; does not gate queries, deletions, or
explicit verbs (a `build` while paused asks). Survives restart by
construction; carried into a fresh file on sideline. Plus the verbs residue:
`purge`, and confirm tokens that quote cost (rebuild confirm carries the item
count so a stale confirmation cannot authorize a bigger job). R1-vs-R22
resolved in the user's favor, disclosed: "paused since <date>".

## Exit criteria
- [ ] pause survives restart and gates auto_build; queries still answer
- [ ] status says "paused since <date>"
- [ ] confirm-token verbs (`reset`, `rebuild`, `purge`) with quoted costs
- [ ] PR opened upstream; outcome recorded here
